From bfe2ee3e898cedbf73a7d73d123c91a12e0b76a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeong, Heon" <blmarket@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:10:22 -0700
Subject: Fix memory leak when a style is not terminated

format_draw() starts a screen write context for each of its screens, and
a context holds a collected item from the moment screen_write_start()
takes one off the free list. The one exit that does not go through the
screen_write_stop() loop is the "no terminating ]" case, which jumps
straight to freeing the screens, so every context's items are lost rather
than being handed back to the free list.

The string is a user format and the draw happens on every redraw, so this
grows for as long as the format stays wrong. A server drawing a status
format of "left#[fg=red" ten times exits under AddressSanitizer with

    Direct leak of 7296 byte(s) in 76 object(s) allocated from:
        #2 screen_write_get_citem screen-write.c:73
        #3 screen_write_clearline screen-write.c:1647
        #4 format_draw format-draw.c:750

and more of the same out of screen_write_start(); none with this applied.

Applies to 3.7b at a different offset; the branch and the TOTAL contexts
around it are the same there.
---
 format-draw.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/format-draw.c b/format-draw.c
--- a/format-draw.c
+++ b/format-draw.c
@@ -820,6 +820,8 @@ format_draw(struct screen_write_ctx *octx, const struct grid_cell *base,
 			    cp + 2);
 			TAILQ_FOREACH_SAFE(fr, &frs, entry, fr1)
 			    format_free_range(&frs, fr);
+			for (i = 0; i < TOTAL; i++)
+				screen_write_stop(&ctx[i]);
 			goto out;
 		}
 		tmp = xstrndup(cp + 2, end - (cp + 2));
